<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 352 0 R
/E (Rule-Based vs. Data-Driven: Traditional code uses fixed rules \("If X, do Y"\). AI works differently: instead of hardcoding every rule, we feed it data and examples so it finds patterns on its own.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
79 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 353 0 R
/E (The Training Process: Just like a child learning what an apple is by seeing hundreds of apples, machine learning algorithms process thousands of sample images to recognize visual features \(edges, colors, ratios\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 354 0 R
